 * GENERATED FILE - exported from CloudKit with `cktool export-schema`. Do not hand-edit.
 *
 * To change the schema: edit it here, run `validate-schema`, `import-schema`, then re-export over
 * this file so the committed version matches what the server actually stores.
 *
 * Development and Production are separate. An import only touches Development - deploy to Production
 * from the CloudKit Dashboard ("Deploy Schema Changes") or your App Store build will not see it.
 *
 * Production record types and fields are permanent once deployed: you can add later, never remove.
 *
 * The reasoning behind the shape of this schema - why no BOOLEAN fields, why Comment and DevComment
 * are separate record types, why Report is world-readable but Follow is not, why only `title` is
 * SEARCHABLE - is in README.md under "Index checklist" and "Privacy".
